From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fco Javier Felix <ffelix@inode64.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:20:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drivers/ietf-mib.c: also read UPS-MIB line tables indexed
 from 0

Some RFC 1628 agents (an RTCS 03.02.00 card, for one) number the
upsInputTable, upsOutputTable and upsBypassTable rows from 0 instead
of 1, so the single-phase voltages, currents, powers and load were
never published. Read index .0 as well. Whichever instance does not
answer is disabled at startup, and the .1 entry stays last so that it
wins on an agent answering both.

That card returns 0 for the input current, input power and output
power, which it does not measure, so those three .0 entries treat 0
as invalid. The bypass current and power keep their zeros: 0 is the
normal reading while the load runs on the inverter.

Bump IETF_MIB_VERSION to 1.56.
---
Upstream: not submitted yet. Overlay copy of the commit proposed to NUT.

 drivers/ietf-mib.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/ietf-mib.c b/drivers/ietf-mib.c
index 7ab83effa..e2f168129 100644
--- a/drivers/ietf-mib.c
+++ b/drivers/ietf-mib.c
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 
 #include "ietf-mib.h"
 
-#define IETF_MIB_VERSION	"1.55"
+#define IETF_MIB_VERSION	"1.56"
 
 /* SNMP OIDs set */
 #define IETF_OID_UPS_MIB	"1.3.6.1.2.1.33.1."
@@ -148,18 +148,28 @@ static snmp_info_t ietf_mib[] = {
